  "Currency": "Kaen Mane",
  "Custom tier": "Kastom Level",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous i ripotim abaotem wan raeting wea oli pulum bak (retracted) long Journal of Medical Ethics, wea i gat plande fol refarens wea AI i halusinetim — witim fol yunivesiti afiliesen an fol imel adres wea oli no wok nomoa — wea raeta ia hem oli sei hem i no fiksim yet, iven afta oli givim hem jans blong fiksim ol pruf. Stori ia i putum diswan agens Bioethics, wea otomatik jekim blong refarens bae i bin kajim problem ia; hem i agiu sei trufala problem hem i no teknoloji blong faendemaot (wan komenta i ranim wan skrip an faendemaot ol fol sitesen insaed lesin wan minit), be hem i wok blong ol rivyua wea no pem olketa, an olketa insentiv blong pablisim wea i pemem spid moa winim kwaeti jekim.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Fri-Raedim Data Agens Valu Blong AI Wea I Rijim Trilion Dola",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis i sajestim wan rigyuleta olsem stael blong FINRA, blong olketa rilis blong frontia moddel: olketa laebo bae oli submitim ol moddel blong rivyu, kasem 30 dei bifo oli rilisim, volantri fastaem, witim wan pat i go kasem komplaens wea i mandetori long maket blong US.",
  "Denied": "No-Oke",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Template Blong Statim Polisi Wea Yu Save Deployim",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Template blong statim polisi wea yu save deployim, long /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — wan minimol statik sait wetem full level wea masin save readim, redi blong Cloudflare Pages o eni statik host.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Fasin Blong Deployim Olketa Polisi Wea Masin Save Readim Long Sait Blong Yu",
  "Disclaimer": "Diskleima",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "I difren long UI blong man, SEO, o simpol API, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer i givim olketa websaet wan akitekja wea i fesim masin: wan Manifest Level (ples blong statim olsem /llms.txt an /ai/manifest.json), wan Corpus Level (save wea masin save readim), wan Kapabiliti Level (olketa tul wea ejent save kolem), an wan Gavenens Level (wea i kamaot from, laesensing, vesin namba). Statik fastaem, save apgredim i go long API an MCP. Notis: long pepa ia, AICL i minim akitekja blong ingestion; long olketa pej blong protokol blong sait ia, AICL i minim Level Blong Laesensing Blong AI Kontent.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Dokumen",
  "Docs / Examples": "Dokumen / Eksampol",
  "Document library": "Laebrari Blong Dokumen",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "Waswe, AI i gat raet — an wanem framing nao i mekesens trufala?",
  "Download": "Daonlod",
  "Draft status": "Stetas Blong Draft",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Demo blong lanem save: HMAC-SHA256 witim wan sikret wea oli sherem, i soem olketa token blong laesens wea fitim risik, gat en-taem, an yu save verifaem. Olketa token blong prodaksen sud saenim asimetrikoli, witim pablik kii blong pablisa wea yu save faendem aninit long /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Eit moa /topics entri, distaem wan AI ejent i risejim, i no man i kiuretim wetem hand — semfala rul olsem bifo: evri sos oli pulum an konfemem i stap laef, olketa sammari i orijinol parafres, bifo eni samting oli adem. 14 entri oltugeta.",
  "Email": "Imel",
  "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model": "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model",
  "Empirical Research": "Empirikol Risej",
  "English edition →": "Inglis Edisen →",
  "Ensure openness is machine-executable — so goodwill is not discarded as legal uncertainty.": "Mekem sua sei openes i save ranem tru masin — mekem gudfala tingting i no lus olsem legol antaseten.",
  "Epistemology": "Epistemoloji",
